    "editorial": {
      "title": "cPGuard update-channel breach exposes root-level server secrets",
      "summary": "OPSSHIELD says attackers used its cPGuard update channel to send a malicious update on November 2. Its later disclosure describes roughly 70 minutes of malicious distribution and exposure of root-level secrets, superseding the vendor’s earlier account.",
      "why_it_matters": "A clean update cannot invalidate credentials copied before cleanup. The vendor’s earlier and later accounts describe different investigation stages; their scope estimates should not be combined.",
